Contact box design unified across the site (2026-09-22)
Goal (PM, from two screenshots): the Corporate Contact box and the About
page's "Get in touch" box should share the same design (colours), even
though their fields differ; remove "How can we help?" from the Corporate
message box specifically, not site-wide; the About box's nonprofit-status
line looked "squashed and inelegant."
Found: three different looks were in use across nine ContactForm-using
pages — a plain grey-bordered card (six pages), the pink-accent-border
card (Corporate only, Ways to Support), and a pale-teal panel (About).
Built: ContactForm.astro — the pink-accent style (white background, 1px
pink border, 5px on the left, no shadow) is now the component's own
DEFAULT non-compact card, so it applies automatically to every page using
the plain form (Auditions, Volunteer, School Play in a Box, Stories on
Stage main + each production's booking form) with no changes needed on
those page files; added an optional messagePlaceholder prop (default "How
can we help?") so one instance can override or blank it without affecting
the rest. about.astro — .contact-card switched from pale-teal/grey-border
to the same white/pink-accent style; .nonprofit-note given a
margin-bottom (it had margin-top only, so the form's first field sat
jammed directly underneath it). ways-to-support.astro — Corporate form
passes messagePlaceholder="" to drop its placeholder only.
Deliberately unchanged: the Classes & Camps "Questions?" card, which sits
in a 3-card grid matching its neighbours (Studio Classes, Camps) — giving
it its own border would have broken that grid's consistency instead of
fixing anything.
Tested: computed-style check on six pages confirmed the new border/
background; corporate placeholder confirmed empty string; About gap
between the nonprofit line and the first field label confirmed at 24px
(was 0). Before/after mockup rendered on the real site with real fonts.

